    {
      "id": "04-carbs",
      "index": 3,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "carbs",
      "text": "72.1 grams of carbs. Starch is 61.7 grams, providing the grain's main source of energy. Sugar is 0 grams, but the glycemic index is still 63, which is only moderate. This is a good lesson: low sugar does not automatically mean low glycemic, because starch also becomes glucose. For grains, carb behaviour matters more than carb amount.",
      "textSha256": "c605f2942ec1d702cd49947d9cd8086d5de46f8f4d24e3ddc56ee115af215868",
      "characterCount": 335,
      "byteLength": 313931,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 19.592,
      "audioFile": "/studio-data/uploads/narration/farro/04-carbs.mp3",
